    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are the base class and a helper), and it passes \u2014 including the new assertion on `$.timezone`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` derivation on the `Owner` response, mapping locality/region \u2192 IANA timezone via the fixed table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string field to the `Owner` schema (right after `locality`), documenting the fixed region-to-timezone table. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", expression = \"java(timezone(owner))\")` and a `timezone(Owner owner)` method that derives the region via the existing `locality(owner)` and maps it: `NSW \u2192 Australia/Sydney`, `VIC \u2192 Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD \u2192 Australia/Brisbane`, returning `null` for any other region (e.g. `UNKNOWN`), so the field is simply absent then.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` test confirms an owner in Sydney (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) returns `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`.",
