    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `timezone` method fits the file's established pattern exactly: like every other derived field (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, \u2026), it's a `default` method on the interface with a null-guard, a descriptive Javadoc stating the table and the null-when-absent behavior, and a corresponding `@Mapping(... expression ...)` entry declared in the same block.\n\nNotably good structural choices:\n- It **reuses `locality(owner)`** to obtain the region rather than re-deriving it from `customerCode`, so the region-extraction logic lives in exactly one place and `timezone` composes on top of it \u2014 the right unit for the logic.\n- The fixed region-to-timezone table is expressed as an idiomatic Java `switch` expression with an explicit `default -> null`, which reads naturally and mirrors the small-lookup style used elsewhere.\n- The OpenAPI `timezone` schema entry sits alongside `locality`, marked `readOnly` with an example and a description matching the sibling derived fields.\n\nNothing is duplicated, and the mapper isn't becoming a catch-all beyond the pattern it already follows for derived presentation fields. A maintainer of this codebase would find it natural.",
